  m_Name: 1944
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Japanese Occupation of Singapore During WWII 1942-1945
  info: "During World War II, Japanese forces invade Singapore in a swift and decisive
    campaign, marking one of Britain\u2019s worst military defeats. Renaming it \"Syonan-to\"
    or \"Light of the South Island,\" the Japanese impose harsh military rule. The
    occupation is marked by atrocities, including the Sook Ching Massacre, where
    thousands of ethnic Chinese are executed. This period deeply impacts Singaporeans,
    fostering a collective desire to end colonial domination and secure self-determination."
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 601d3872cb0a44da8847a6ead025f1aa, type: 3}
